    "body": "This is causing a conflict with the existing definition at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#event-input which is causing the build failure.\r\n\r\nThere are two ways to resolve it. We can either:\r\n\r\n1. Remove this line, so that we continue to have two definitions of the `input` event in the spec ecosystem, one in HTML and one in UI Events. (This is what I was advising in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6743#discussion_r646820717.)\r\n2. Link the `input` event in the event index to UI Events's definition, i.e. change line 127269 from a `<dfn>` to a `<span>`.\r\n3. Remove HTML's definition of the `input` event entirely, i.e. remove lines 127268-127272.\r\n\r\nAt first I preferred (1) since, as mentioned in #6743, UI Event's event definitions are bad. However I see upon reviewing that we've acceded to their bad definitions for many other cases, e.g. `click` has chosen (2) and `mouseleave` has chosen (3).\r\n\r\nSo, probably (2) is best.",
    "created_at": "2022-06-08T16:38:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-08T16:39:33Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7992#discussion_r892606784",
